paths: tests/conformance/contract.sc specs/conformance-perf.md
scope: |
  contract.sc's own header has carried this TODO since 2026-07-14: "add memo (F2) + batch lanes (F4)
  like run.sc". run.sc got batching; the corpus gate never did — and the gate is the one that could
  not reach a verdict for 13 runs.

  MEASURED cost of one gate run, in cold JVM starts:
    INT ~699  (214 example cases x2 for the determinism check + ~271 conformance cases with a golden)
    JS   485
    v2   485
    total ~1669
  Batching INT alone removes ~699 of them. That is the same cost that produced both the 60-minute
  timeout and the host memory pressure Sergiy had to kill by hand.

  SCOPE — INT ONLY, deliberately:
   - `run-batch --v1` dispatches the SAME `run --v1` path per file, just in one JVM, so the lane's
     meaning is unchanged.
   - JS would mean swapping `run-js` for `emit-js | node`. That REDEFINES what the lane tests, and a
     correctness gate is the wrong place to do that quietly.
   - v2 cannot be batched at all today: `run-batch` exists only on `ssc-tools`, and the gate's v2
     lane is `bin/ssc run --v2` (StandardMain), which has no such command. Separate task.

  SEMANTICS — batch accelerates PASS, never classifies failure. Classification uses the exit code
  (124 -> TIMEOUT, non-zero -> FAIL) and a batch gives one process for many cases, so: if a case's
  batched output equals the golden it is PASS; anything else — different output, missing section, a
  case that called exit() and killed the batch — falls through to the existing per-case run and is
  classified exactly as today. No classification rule changes.

  KNOWN RISK, stated not hidden: one JVM means cross-case state (globals, plugin registry) can leak,
  so a batched PASS is marginally weaker evidence than an isolated one. run.sc has accepted that
  trade since F4; this records it rather than inheriting it silently, and `--no-batch` /
  SSC_CONTRACT_NO_BATCH=1 turn it off for a run that must be isolated.
next: port BATCH_MARK/splitBatch/batchLane from run.sc, wire golden() + the int lane, verify a
  batched run and a --no-batch run agree case-for-case
